SUMMARY:Botany: Online (4-sessions)
DESCRIPTION:with Matt Jones\, Extension Agent – Horticulture\, NC Cooperative Extension \nDates: Fridays\, September 11\, 18\, 25\, and October 2\, 2026 (4-sessions)\nTime: 10:00 AM – 12:00 PM\nFee: $190 ($170 Members) \nCourse Format: Online via Zoom. Includes pre-recorded lectures shared in advance of four live Zoom sessions with the instructor and fellow learners. \nPlants are the foundation of every ecosystem\, and exploring their structure\, function\, and diversity reveals the remarkable complexity of plants and the ways they shape the world around us. This course introduces the fundamental principles of botany and provides a foundation for anyone interested in developing a deeper understanding of plants. \nOpen to the general public. This course is part of the Certificate in Native Plants and Certificate in Botanical Art & Illustration programs. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/botany-online-course/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Learn
END:VEVENT
