SUMMARY:Sculpture in the Garden Preview Party
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the Preview Party for the 38th annual Sculpture in the Garden exhibit! \nSculpture in the Garden (September 13 – December 6\, 2026) unites the work of local artists with the landscapes of the North Carolina Botanical Garden. \nAt the Preview Party on Saturday\, September 12\, you’ll get first viewing of the show (and the first chance to purchase pieces)\, meet the artists\, and enjoy a catered reception. \nWe’ll announce the winners of Best in Show and Honorable Mentions\, selected by a jurist\, and you’ll be able to cast your vote for the People’s Choice Award. \nTickets are $40 per person; half of each ticket price supports Sculpture in the Garden and is tax-deductible. Event is rain or shine. Attendance is limited\, so register today! \n\nGet tickets\n* * * * * \nAfter the Preview Party on September 12\, Sculpture in the Garden is free and open to the public during normal Garden hours (Tuesdays through Sundays\, 9 a.m. to 5 p.m.). Learn more and plan your visit
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/sculpture-in-the-garden-preview-party/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Special Events
