SUMMARY:Tour of Coker Arboretum
DESCRIPTION:Discover this five-acre gem in the heart of the UNC campus. Established in 1903\, Coker Arboretum is part of the North Carolina Botanical Garden and features a wide variety of plantings\, including flowering trees and shrubs\, bulbs\, and perennials. Join a Coker Arboretum curator for a walking tour of this historic garden. Offered each season\, every tour reveals something new as the Arboretum changes throughout the year. \nFee: $10 ($8 Members) \nLocation: Meets at Coker Arboretum on the UNC-Chapel Hill campus \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/tour-of-coker-arboretum/
LOCATION:Coker Arboretum\, 399 E. Cameron Avenue\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
CATEGORIES:Hikes and Tours,Learn
