SUMMARY:Lunchbox Talk: North Carolina Botanical Garden - A Wildlife Haven
DESCRIPTION:with Mary Sonis\, Naturalist\, Photographer\, Writer \nLocation: In-Person at the North Carolina Botanical Garden\, Reeves Auditorium \nFree; preregistration required \nJoin local naturalist and wildlife photographer Mary Sonis for a visual journey into the remarkable wildlife of the North Carolina Botanical Garden. Through stunning photographs and engaging stories\, explore the rich biodiversity supported by native plant habitats. From songbirds and pollinators to elusive mammals\, discover the fascinating creatures that call the Garden home. \nBlending humor\, keen observation\, and natural history\, Mary invites you to see familiar landscapes with fresh eyes and reminds us that extraordinary wildlife can be found right in our own backyards. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/lunchbox-talk-north-carolina-botanical-garden-a-wildlife-haven-hybrid/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Learn,Lunchbox Talks
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncbg.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/963/2026/08/foxkit_Sonis.jpg
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
