SUMMARY:Nature Tales: Monarch Magic (AM session)
DESCRIPTION:Ages: 3-7 with participating adult\nFee: $5 per child (No fee for Members and families receiving SNAP benefits) \nFlit\, flutter\, fly… it’s monarch time! Discover the amazing journey monarch butterflies make each year through stories and songs. Then\, we’ll explore the gardens in search of hungry caterpillars\, butterflies\, and the plants they love to eat. \nNature Tales is a monthly storytime series led by our youth education staff that invites young children and their caregivers to explore the natural world through stories\, songs\, and hands-on activities. Each program features a nature-inspired theme\, followed by a guided exploration of the Garden where families can discover the wonders of the living world together. \nThis program takes place in our beautiful new Wilkinson Outdoor Classroom! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/nature-tales-monarch-magic/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Learn
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncbg.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/963/2026/08/Monarch-butterfly-fresh-emergence_edited_Nik_310w.jpg
